  "summary": "IcePeony is a China-nexus APT active since at least 2023 that gains access via SQL injection against public web servers, then deploys webshells and two custom malware families: the IIS module IceCache (Go, derived from reGeorge/reGeorgGo) and the passive service backdoor IceEvent, which share XOR-encoded C2 protocol and PDB paths under user 'power'. The actor uses open-source tooling (sqlmap, ProxyChains, Mimikatz, Diamorphine, craXcel, WmiExec, suo5) and a customized Stowaway variant called StaX. Detection can key on PDB paths, HTTP X-Cmd/X-Token headers and the 16-byte XOR key shared by both malware families.",
